Task: Display underlying commands in verbose mode (Phase 3, Task 1)

Summary:
Added print_verbose() calls to display the underlying commands being
executed when verbosity is set to VERBOSE. In test_runner.py, the full
Godot command (binary --path project_root <args>) is printed before each
run_godot() call (headless import and GUT test run). In lint_runner.py,
the file being linted is printed before each lint_code() call. In
format_runner.py, the file being formatted is printed before each
format_code() call. Also added an autouse _reset_verbosity fixture to
conftest.py to prevent verbosity state leakage between tests.

Files modified:
- src/gd_tools/test_runner.py: Added output.print_verbose() before both
  run_godot() calls, showing the full command with binary, --path, and args
- src/gd_tools/lint_runner.py: Added output.print_verbose() before
  lint_code(), showing "Linting: <file_path>"
- src/gd_tools/format_runner.py: Added output import and
  output.print_verbose() before format_code(), showing "Formatting: <file_path>"
- tests/unit/conftest.py: Added autouse _reset_verbosity fixture
- tests/unit/test_test_runner.py: Added 2 verbose mode tests
- tests/unit/test_lint_runner.py: Added 2 verbose mode tests
- tests/unit/test_format_runner.py: Added 2 verbose mode tests
- conductor/tracks.md: Updated track status to [~] (in progress)

Why:
Users need to see the actual commands being executed for debugging
purposes. The --verbose flag now reveals the underlying Godot/GUT,
gdlint, and gdformat invocations that are otherwise hidden.

